      "parameters": {
        "language": "javaScript",
        "jsCode": "// Each upstream node returns an array of rows, mapped into the central\n// customers shape and tagged with the right product + kind.\n//\n// 2026-08-20: the gutted / onalert / merciless fetch nodes were DELETED, not\n// just disabled. All three products were retired or archived in July 2026 and\n// none appears in venture_registry. Their Supabase projects have since been\n// reused (hzadscrqmyilbisexvyz is now full-time, cgkcplcamsijghalintq was\n// plinth/legibility, also retired), so those nodes were pointed at live\n// projects reading tables for products that no longer exist.\n//\n// Fractionl Circle and Fractionl Pulse are the only live sources here. Neither\n// full-time nor any other venture exposes a customer/subscription endpoint yet.\n// Do NOT invent one: add a fetch node plus a mapping block below when a real\n// profiles/subscriptions/waitlist endpoint exists.\nconst circle   = $('Fractionl Circle: subscriptions').all().map(i => i.json).flat();\nconst pulseW   = $('Fractionl Pulse: waitlist').all().map(i => i.json).flat();\n\nconst out = [];\nfor (const r of circle) {\n  const isActive = r.status === 'active' && !r.cancel_at_period_end;\n  out.push({ product: 'fractionl_circle', kind: isActive ? 'paid' : 'churned', email: r.email || null, plan: r.tier || null, stripe_customer_id: r.stripe_customer_id || null, stripe_subscription_id: r.stripe_subscription_id || null, became_paid_at: r.created_at, churned_at: isActive ? null : (r.updated_at || null) });\n}\nfor (const r of pulseW)  out.push({ product: 'fractionl_pulse', kind: 'waitlist',   email: r.email || null, signed_up_at: r.created_at, source: 'waitlist' });\n\nreturn out.map(row => ({ json: row }));\n"
      },
      "id": "68dadcd0-71bf-44ad-a323-2952e2bd337d"
    },
